<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isthmian Games</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Isthmian Games were one of the four Panhellenic festivals of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, held every two years near Corinth in honour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poseidon">Poseidon</a>, with victors crowned with pine or wild celery. In 196 BCE the Roman general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-quinctius-flamininus">Titus Quinctius Flamininus</a> proclaimed the freedom of the Greek cities at the games, and after the Roman destruction of Corinth in 146 BCE they were run by Sicyon until the city was refounded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isthmian-games.jpg" alt="Isthmian Games" width="320" height="296" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stella maris · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:4-panhellenic-games-en.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
